{
 "_doc": "fpf_trimul_v4 launch cells: ONE table. Rows keyed '<cc major.minor>|<triton major.minor>' (exact) and '<cc>|*' (any other triton on that capability; pointer-load cells only). A row's k1/k3 are the (C, D) = (256, 256) no-bias cells; 'overrides' carry the per-shape cells the kernel resolves by k1_C<C>_D<D>[_bias] / k3_... (table.resolve_cfg: first match of C_D_bias, C_D, C_bias, C, else the row's k1/k3). impl='tma' K1 cells (kernels._k1t) and the host-descriptor cells impl='tma2' (K1, kdesc._k1d: incoming planes transposed, both directions one a @ b^T GEMM) / K3 impl='tma' (kdesc._k3d) need triton's tensor-descriptor API (else the next candidate row serves; fp32 input and plane extents below kdesc.N_MIN_DESC always take the pointer / _k1t kernels of the same cell numbers). 'kit_keys': the exact parts where two sweeps measured different (128,128) no-bias cells \u2014 there a kit's own table (FPF_TRIMUL_V4_CELLS) that serves the part serves it (source=kit-table); everywhere else this table's row serves and the kit's table is evidence only, named per part. A capability with no row serves the SAFE cell of opt_core.kernels.safe_settings ('pair_fused:trimul': the capability's row or its any-capability '*' row), named once. 'successors': per override key, the cell this row served before its current one when the change kept the output bytes (the descriptor cells of CHANGELOG 4.4.0 replaced the cells named there): a kit's measured selection of the older cell is a served, named change (opt_core tests/test_trimul_v4_one_table.py), not a divergence. Served rows: status prefix table.SERVED_STATUS_PREFIX. Which engine's measurement supplies each cell: opt_core CHANGES.md 0.5.18.9.",
